Maintainer: Mitsuru Mukaigawara <mitsuru_mukaigawara@g.harvard.edu>
Description: Methods for causal inference with spatio-temporal data. Point
    process tools estimate causal effects over specified spatial and temporal
    windows from treatment and outcome events. Unit-level longitudinal tools estimate
    propensity scores and evaluate or learn stochastic treatment policies for
    discrete spatial or administrative units.
    See Papadogeorgou, et  al. (2022) <doi:10.1111/rssb.12548> and
    Mukaigawara, et al. (2024) <doi:10.31219/osf.io/5kc6f>.
